{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 20}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 105, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the strongest conv on the output-feeding edge with parameter-free pooling removes most of the cell's learned capacity, far worse than replacing skip/none/pool."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 5 is much more damaging when it carried a 3x3 conv than when it carried a weak or empty op."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv from a direct output edge loses substantial capacity, unlike removing skip or pooling (cf. exps 9, 10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Upgrading pooling to a 3x3 conv on the output edge yields a far larger gain than upgrading skip or a 1x1 conv."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding the input-to-output residual where none existed greatly aids optimization, whereas replacing an existing conv with skip loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty edge 3 with a conv adds capacity without sacrificing an existing residual or conv path."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 5 is none, node 2 never reaches the output, so adding a conv on edge 1 has essentially no benefit."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 4 removed, node 1 reaches the output only indirectly, so strengthening edge 0 helps less."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "